       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**. This order is twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults on prescription is **3200 mg/day**. This order is twice that.\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other NSAID toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Was one of these intended?**\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day): a common anti-inflammatory or pain dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2400 mg/day) or **800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg total daily dose**, split into several doses\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean a dose above the standard maximum, tell me the clinical reason and I can add it as a note on the order. I'd still recommend a pharmacist review it first."
      }
     ],
